{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>Let them be consumed</b> — The prayer of the prophet, because they do not acknowledge HaShem and do not understand His deeds. Or he mentioned this because he said: 'I will rejoice in YHWH,' and not so the sinners, for they shall be consumed and lost." "<b>they are no more</b> — The meaning is doubled." "<b>Bless YHWH, my soul</b> — On account of the destruction of the wicked. And he sealed [the psalm] by saying to the maskilim: Hallelujah."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 104, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:20.877763017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}